hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1112","He said: Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, told us on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, he said: I said to Ibn Omar, Have you seen? The two rak'ahs before the morning prayer, should I prolong the recitation during them? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the two rak’ahs before lunch, as if it was the adhan in his ears.”"
"1113","Muhammad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, meaning Ibn al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Sa`id saying: Muhammad ibn Abdul Rahman, that he heard Amra speaking, on the authority of Aisha, and Abu Ammar narrated to us, Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, and Yusuf bin narrated to us Musa, Jarir narrated to us, H. Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj narrated to us, Abu Khaled narrated to us all, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, and this is the hadith of Muhammad ibn al-Walid, that she used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And he prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr. He shortened them to the point that I would say: Did he recite in them the Umm al-Kitab? Abu Ammar said in his hadith: Until I say: Did he recite anything in them?"
